{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>They have a mouth</b> — And the glory of man over all creatures below is in the supernal soul, possessor of speech; therefore he said: 'They have a mouth.' And afterward he mentioned the sensation of the eye and also the ears, for they are the most honored among the senses, and he left the other three." "<b>And the meaning of 'indeed there is no breath (רוח) in their mouth'</b> — The רוח is the body (גוף) that is found in man and beast and bird, belonging to every sentient being, and it is the essence of all sensations; but the idol is less than every sentient thing." "<b>And the meaning of 'in their mouth'</b> — For the breath (רוח) that enters through the mouth gives life; this breath stands in the heart, and when it goes out from the heart it goes out through the mouth; therefore he said: 'in their mouth.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 135, :notes {0 "Reading 'נבראי מטה' as 'creatures below'; possible corruption for 'נבראי המטה' or similar.", 1 "Reading 'העצב' (the idol/image) literally; context is Psalms 135:15–18 on idols."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:50.421123167Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}